# .env.throwaway.example — template for the AGENT automated live-test env source
#
# This is the committed template for `.env.throwaway` — the ISOLATED cluster-env
# source an Agent_Live_Run reads its Proxmox parameters from. Copy it and fill in
# real values for your dedicated THROWAWAY / EPHEMERAL Proxmox cluster:
#
#   cp .env.throwaway.example .env.throwaway
#   $EDITOR .env.throwaway        # fill in the real THROWAWAY endpoint + token
#
# ==========================================================================
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR — READ BEFORE USING
# ==========================================================================
#   * `.env.throwaway` is for the KIRO AGENT's automated live runs (from-scratch
#     bring-ups, `clean_slate` resets, `terraform apply`/`destroy`) against a
#     designated THROWAWAY cluster ONLY.
#   * It is GITIGNORED (it carries a REAL throwaway token) and is NEVER committed.
#   * It is NEVER used in CI / acceptance / production — the agent live-test
#     interlock is a local-development affordance only.
#   * It is DISTINCT from a developer's manual `.env` / `cluster.*.env`. Keeping
#     the agent's env source separate means an automated agent run cannot pick up
#     a developer's manual `.env` pointing at a different (non-throwaway) Proxmox.
#   * The cluster identity (endpoint host + node name) resolved from this file
#     MUST match an entry in `scripts/installer/throwaway-clusters.yml`, or the
#     throwaway guard fails CLOSED and the destructive run is refused.
#
# SECURITY (security-standards.md):
#   * No secret is ever committed to the repo — `.env.throwaway` is gitignored;
#     keep it so. Never put a real token in THIS `.env.throwaway.example`; the
#     values below are obviously-fake placeholders only.
#   * A Proxmox API token has the format:  <user>@<realm>!<token-id>=<uuid>
#   * Use a TEST-cluster token, never production, and never a token with the
#     built-in Administrator role.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cluster env schema — same variables cluster_env.py consumes, so this file can
# be passed as `--env-file .env.throwaway`.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Proxmox API endpoint of the THROWAWAY cluster (scheme/port/path are normalized
# for the allowlist host comparison). Placeholder only — replace with your real
# throwaway cluster endpoint.
PROXMOX_ENDPOINT="https://your-throwaway-cluster.example.invalid:8006/"

# Proxmox API token for the THROWAWAY cluster. Obviously-fake placeholder —
# never commit a real token here.
PROXMOX_API_TOKEN="terraform@pve!ci=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

# Proxmox node name of the THROWAWAY cluster. This exact (trimmed) value must be
# listed as `node_name` in scripts/installer/throwaway-clusters.yml.
PROXMOX_NODE_NAME="your-throwaway-node"

# Base LXC template on the throwaway cluster (stock debian-12-standard per ADR-0003).
PROXMOX_LXC_TEMPLATE="local:vztmpl/debian-12-standard_12.7-1_amd64.tar.zst"

# Optional: storage pool for guest disks. When unset, the installer autodetects
# (local-zfs → local-lvm fallback).
# PROXMOX_DATASTORE_ID="local-zfs"

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator SSH PUBLIC key — REQUIRED for a from-scratch agent bring-up.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STRONGLY RECOMMENDED for any agent-driven from-scratch run. The installer
# injects this PUBLIC key into the freshly-provisioned guests' root account AT
# CREATION time (Terraform initialization.user_account.keys), so Ansible can then
# SSH into them for Phase 3 (the `common` Docker/hardening role) and the OpenBao
# bootstrap.
#
# If you leave this UNSET, the guests are created with NO authorized key and are
# SSH-UNREACHABLE — a from-scratch bring-up then FAILS in Phase 3 with
# `root@10.0.20.x: Permission denied (publickey,password)` (this is a documented
# default, not a bug: see the SVC-07 INSTALL-RUNBOOK §1b and ADR-0004). The
# throwaway guard still authorizes correctly; the failure is purely SSH
# reachability. So for an agent from-scratch acceptance, SET this.
#
# PUBLIC key ONLY — never a private key. The matching PRIVATE key must be
# available to the control node (loaded in the ssh-agent or referenced in
# ~/.ssh/config) so Ansible can authenticate with it. The key is applied at guest
# CREATION only, so after changing it you must clean-slate + re-provision for the
# new guests to pick it up.
#
# Provide EITHER a path to your .pub file:
PROXMOX_SSH_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE="~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub"
# ...or the HCL-list form Terraform reads directly (mutually exclusive with the above):
# TF_VAR_operator_ssh_public_keys='["ssh-ed25519 AAAAPLACEHOLDER-replace-with-your-real-public-key operator@example"]'

# ==========================================================================
# INTERLOCK — NOT a file key. Set it as an ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE per run.
# ==========================================================================
# The agent live-test interlock, AGENT_LIVE_AUTHORIZED, is read from the process
# ENVIRONMENT by the throwaway guard, NOT parsed out of this file. This keeps
# arming a CONSCIOUS, per-invocation act that can never be silently baked into a
# committed file (mirrors the openbao_dev_expose_secrets opt-in philosophy:
# off by default, never a committed default, never in CI/acceptance/production).
#
# Arm a single agent live run by exporting it on the command line, e.g.:
#
#   AGENT_LIVE_AUTHORIZED=1 ~/venv/devinfra/bin/ansible-playbook \
#     -i ansible/inventory/localhost.yml \
#     ansible/playbooks/svc-07-bootstrap.yml \
#     -e cluster_env_file=.env.throwaway
#
# Optional per-service NARROWING — restrict the arm to specific services only
# (it can only narrow, never broaden, the global arm). Also an ENV var, e.g.:
#
#   AGENT_LIVE_AUTHORIZED=1 AGENT_LIVE_AUTHORIZED_SERVICES=svc07 \
#     ~/venv/devinfra/bin/ansible-playbook ...
#
# Do NOT add AGENT_LIVE_AUTHORIZED=... as a line in .env.throwaway; the committed
# template deliberately never does, honoring "never a committed default".
